      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.0,
      "end_seconds": 160.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.48,
      "end_seconds": 165.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "not to to my knowledge, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.42,
      "end_seconds": 170.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.54,
      "end_seconds": 175.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "I have asthma"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.88,
      "end_seconds": 183.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.44,
      "text": "alright, asthma, that matches what I have here. Anything surgical in your history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.43,
      "end_seconds": 194.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.2,
      "text": "yes I had a bunion operation six years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.78,
      "end_seconds": 214.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "let's talk a little about your daily life and habits"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.39,
      "end_seconds": 228.5,
      "duration_seconds": 12.11,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I walk the dog every morning. I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 229.45,
      "end_seconds": 241.34,
      "duration_seconds": 11.89,
      "text": "Okay so the vitals from earlier. Height 167 centimetres blood pressure 109 over 77. Pulse 82 SpO2 98 percent on room air weight 71 kilos temperature is 36.7 degrees respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.29,
      "end_seconds": 243.99,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.16,
      "end_seconds": 249.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.14,
      "end_seconds": 253.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "I'll listen to your chest now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.37,
      "end_seconds": 273.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Your chest is clear and your oxygen level is normal at rest and after walking."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.02,
      "end_seconds": 281.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Right all finished thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.97,
      "end_seconds": 315.24,
      "duration_seconds": 25.27,
      "text": "let me tell you where I've got to. I think we're dealing with breathlessness from low fitness at this stage. It could also be mild asthma, so we'll keep that open. Build up to thirty minutes of brisk walking five days a week. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.29,
      "end_seconds": 319.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Okay, makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.88,
      "end_seconds": 324.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "that's everything on my side anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
